# Nothing pnpm-specific belongs in this file.
#
# pnpm 11 reads its own settings from `pnpm-workspace.yaml` — `allowBuilds`,
# `minimumReleaseAgeExclude`, `node-linker`, hoisting patterns, all of it. Settings written
# here are ignored without an error, which is worse than a failure: this file used to carry
# `node-linker=hoisted`, and the repo has been installed, built, packaged and verified
# against pnpm's default *isolated* layout the whole time (`pnpm config get node-linker`
# reports undefined; `node_modules/.pnpm/` exists). Put the setting in
# `pnpm-workspace.yaml` if it is ever actually wanted, and expect the tree to be relaid out.
#
# Registry credentials and npm-level settings — the things npm itself reads — are still fine
# here. There are none, and none should be committed.
